message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Health Insurance Pricing: Prediction Methods, Churn Risk and AI Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible data science case for health insurance pricing. The project
  compares K-Means clustering, linear regression, a formally selected non-linear
  model (Kernel Ridge) and an AI-generated Random Forest workflow on the same
  public Kaggle dataset, and connects expense prediction to premium pricing,
  churn risk and profit for both new and current customers.
